  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Youth Development Activity</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Turkmenistan):  In FY 2022 the Youth Development Activity (YDA) will focus on supporting youth from primary school through to their first jobs, to become productive, well-adjusted members of the Turkmen workforce and their communities. This activity blends education, entrepreneurship, civil society, and development initiatives to provide a holistic approach to supporting Turkmen youth. YDA will use FY 2022 funds to create opportunities for Turkmen youth to acquire marketable skills by arranging hard and soft skills courses at local educational organizations with a special focus on marginalized groups.  It will assist training centers to make their curricula more market oriented and create sustainable linkages between educational organizations and industries.  YDA will partner with local NGOs implement programs that support expiring youth in starting their own businesses and carrying out projects that contribute to economic development of their communities. YDA will utilize the USAID Youth in Development Policy and support areas that are critical to supporting Turkmen youth&apos;s educational needs. This activity will support ICS Mission Objective 1.2: Contribute to GoTM digitalization and modernization efforts to improve Turkmenistan&apos;s economy, government, and society by providing young entrepreneurs with the skills they need to succeed; thus, contributing to the economic stability and by empowering youth to be active civic leaders through training, and events. The activity will contribute to the U.S. Strategy on Central Asia Objective 1 by equipping youth with the critical thinking skills to recognize a clear path to maintaining individual sovereignty and achieving economic independence and Objective 6 by investing in a network of future leaders who will have the skills and knowledge to advocate for an enabling environment for business that is transparent, open, fair, and attractive to investors. This activity also supports CAATSA Objective 7: economic resilience.</narrative>
  </description>
